# Coach speech (Spanish): the appraisal after the game (src/coach/appraisal.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/appraisal.lang (its header documents every placeholder).
#
# Notes for Spanish:
# - Always positive, never blaming; the coach says "tú", the player's gender is unknown (no
#   "preparado", "listo"...: "ya puedes pasar al nivel ..."). Spain usage: the present perfect for
#   the result and the totals of the game just finished ("has ganado", "has capturado 3 piezas");
#   the preterite for one moment of it that the coach recalls ("La jugada clave fue...",
#   "En la jugada 12 encontraste...", "¿Te acuerdas de...? Ganaste...", "dejé mi alfil").
# - {text} for a phase carries its article ("la apertura", "el medio juego", "el final"); for a draw
#   it is the reason with its preposition ("por repetición", "de mutuo acuerdo"), said after "Tablas".
#   {level} is the level name in quotes («Principiante»), said after "el nivel". {theme} is an
#   infinitive phrase ("vigilar los dobles ataques"), said after a colon.
#   Never put "a" or "de" right before {text} or {opening}: "a el" / "de el" cannot contract.
# - {opening:def} = the opening name with its article ("la defensa siciliana", "el gambito de dama").
# - {moves:move} = "24 jugadas"; {n:captured} = "3 piezas capturadas"; {m:check} = "2 jaques"
#   (counted nouns of common.lang). A number said on its own (a move number, an accuracy without
#   "por ciento") takes {x:num} so that 100 says "cien", not "ciento": "la jugada {n:num}",
#   "Precisión {acc:num}", "un {acc:num} por ciento"; "{acc} por ciento" says "ciento por ciento".

